      "body": "### Project URL\n\nhttps://github.com/andrehora/gh-langs\n\n### Category\n\nOther\n\n### Project Title\n\nLanguages and extensions known to GitHub. Extracted from Linguist.\n\n### Project Description\n\nHello guys, \n\nI needed a tool to easily explore the languages and extensions known to GitHub and to collect basic language data.\nAs I couldn't find such a tool, I implemented `gh-langs` on the top of GitHub Linguist data:\n\n- Webapp: https://andrehora.github.io/gh-langs\n- Dataset: https://github.com/andrehora/gh-langs\n\nAny feedback is welcomed :)\n\n---\n\n### Fun Fact: Languages with the most extensions\n\nSee: [stats_languages_by_extensions.csv](https://github.com/andrehora/gh-langs/blob/main/data/stats_languages_by_extensions.csv)\n\n| Language | Type | Extensions |\n|----------|------|------------|\n| XML | data | 110 |\n| Roff | markup | 28 |\n| JavaScript | programming | 25 |\n| GLSL | programming | 23 |\n| Ruby | programming | 22 |\n| JSON | data | 21 |\n| C++ | programming | 20 |\n| Roff Manpage | markup | 20 |\n| JSON with Comments | data | 18 |\n| Python | programming | 17 |\n\n### Highlights\n\n- Comprehensive dataset of language names, extensions, aliases, and filenames extracted from [GitHub Linguist](https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist). \n- Data is extracted from [languages.yml](https://github.com/github-linguist/linguist/blob/main/lib/linguist/languages.yml).\n- Explore the data: https://andrehora.github.io/gh-langs/\n\n### Example Code\n\n```markdown\n\n```\n\n### Screenshots or Demo Videos\n\n_No response_",
